# Citation metadata in the Citation File Format (CFF) 1.2.0. GitHub reads this file to offer
# "Cite this repository" on the repository page.
#
# It describes the version named below. At each release, update `version` and
# `date-released` (the day the release is tagged; correct it if the tag lands on another
# day). Only the concept DOI is given: it never changes and always leads to the newest
# release, so this file needs no edit after Zenodo has archived a release. The version DOI
# of each release is on its Zenodo page.
#
# The tools and databases FunFlux runs are not repeated here. Their complete list, with the
# references, is the documentation page "Citation and references" (docs/about/citation.md).
#
# When a repository holds both files, Zenodo takes the metadata of each release's record
# from .zenodo.json, not from this file. Keep the title, version and authors the same in both.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FunFlux, please cite it as below, and also cite the tools and databases whose output you used (see https://iLivius.github.io/FunFlux/about/citation/)."
title: "FunFlux: Integrated workflow for fungal genome assembly and annotation"
abstract: >-
  FunFlux is a Snakemake workflow for fungal whole-genome sequencing data. It
  takes a fungal isolate from raw reads, or from an assembly made elsewhere,
  through assembly, contamination and mitochondrion screening, quality control,
  ITS taxonomy, repeat masking, gene prediction and functional annotation, with
  one MultiQC report per run. Version 2.0.0 brings together the earlier FunFlux
  1.x, Funnotator and FunFluxL workflows as four modes of one workflow: Illumina
  paired-end reads, Oxford Nanopore or PacBio HiFi long reads, a hybrid of
  Illumina and long reads, and genomes already assembled.
type: software
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-03
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/iLivius/FunFlux"
url: "https://iLivius.github.io/FunFlux/"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.13612159

authors:
  - family-names: Antonielli
    given-names: Livio
    affiliation: AIT Austrian Institute of Technology
  - family-names: Brader
    given-names: Günter
    affiliation: AIT Austrian Institute of Technology

keywords:
  - fungal genomics
  - whole-genome sequencing
  - Snakemake
  - genome assembly
  - genome annotation
  - gene prediction
  - ITS barcode
  - secondary metabolites
  - antifungal resistance
  - Illumina
  - Oxford Nanopore
  - PacBio HiFi
